"answer": "Project Zenith is a multi-faceted initiative with evolving definitions and phases. Initially introduced by Alex as a data analytics project with a $500,000 budget and Sarah Tan as lead, it has since expanded to include strategic partnerships with TechInnovate for AI research. The project has seen team expansion with five new members specializing in cybersecurity and cloud architecture. Key milestones include the successful completion of the testing phase and the successful testing of a secure file sharing prototype, with user interface enhancements planned for October. Security protocols have been updated to include multi-factor authentication and encryption at rest, effective January next year. Additionally, the compliance plan's budget was increased to $55,000. One email also describes 'Project Zenith' as a set of structured email practices aimed at improving communication efficiency, involving priority-based structuring and requiring team confirmation."
